---
import FAQ from '../FAQ.astro';
import { faqs, benchmarkTiers } from './calculatorData';
---

<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 space-y-16">
  
  {/* Useful Introductory Content */}
  <div class="prose prose-ink dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">
      What is Return on Investment (ROI)?
    </h2>
    <p class="text-body text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Return on Investment (ROI)</strong> is a universal financial metric used to evaluate the efficiency, net gain, and overall profitability of an expenditure relative to its initial cost. Whether you are analyzing stock market portfolios, real estate purchases, business equipment, or digital ad campaigns, calculating ROI provides a clear percentage score of your financial performance.
    </p>
    <p class="text-body text-base leading-relaxed">
      Using a reliable <strong>Return on Investment Calculator</strong> allows business leaders, financial analysts, and digital marketers to compare completely different asset classes and marketing channels on an equal footing. Instead of judging performance by gross revenue alone, ROI focuses on net profit generated per dollar invested.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* ROI Formulas Section */}
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Mathematical Framework</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mt-1">The ROI Formula: How to Calculate ROI</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Understanding the mathematical formulas behind standard ROI, marketing ROI, and annualized returns (CAGR).</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 not-prose">
      {/* Standard ROI Formula */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-3 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>📈</span> Standard ROI Formula
          </h3>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-muted bg-canvas-soft px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-hairline">Cumulative</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Measures total percentage gain or loss over the entire holding period of an investment.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-xl border border-hairline-soft font-mono text-xs text-center font-bold text-ink">
          ROI (%) = <span class="text-primary">[ (Final Return - Initial Investment) / Initial Investment ]</span> × 100
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Marketing ROI Formula */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-3 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>🎯</span> Marketing ROI Formula
          </h3>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-muted bg-canvas-soft px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-hairline">Margin Integrated</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Factors in Cost of Goods Sold (COGS) to isolate true net campaign profitability.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-xl border border-hairline-soft font-mono text-xs text-center font-bold text-ink">
          mROI (%) = <span class="text-primary">[ ((Revenue × Margin %) - Ad Spend) / Ad Spend ]</span> × 100
        </div>
      </div>

      {/* Annualized ROI Formula */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-3 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>📅</span> Annualized ROI (CAGR)
          </h3>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-muted bg-canvas-soft px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-hairline">Per Year</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Normalizes multi-year returns into an equivalent compound annual growth rate.
        </p>
        <div class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft rounded-xl border border-hairline-soft font-mono text-xs text-center font-bold text-ink">
          Annualized ROI = <span class="text-primary">[ (Final Return / Initial Cost)^(1 / Years) - 1 ]</span> × 100
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Explanation of Inputs Section */}
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Calculator Documentation</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mt-1">Explanation of Calculator Inputs</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">A detailed breakdown of every variable used in our ROI calculation engine.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 not-prose">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Initial Investment (Capital Outlay / Ad Spend)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed pl-8">
          The total upfront monetary amount invested. In financial assets, this includes the purchase price, commissions, and setup costs. In digital marketing, this represents your total advertising expenditure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Final Return (Total Value / Revenue Generated)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed pl-8">
          The total gross proceeds received at the end of the investment period or campaign. This encompasses sold asset value, total dividends collected, or total gross e-commerce sales generated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Gross Profit Margin (%) <span class="text-[10px] font-normal text-muted">(Marketing Mode)</span></h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed pl-8">
          The percentage of sales revenue remaining after deducting Cost of Goods Sold (COGS), inventory, and shipping costs. E.g., a 40% margin implies that 60% of revenue goes toward product production and fulfillment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Investment Duration (Years or Months)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed pl-8">
          The time horizon over which the investment was held. Providing a duration unlocks <strong>Annualized ROI (CAGR)</strong>, enabling accurate comparisons between short-term trades and multi-year holdings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline space-y-2 md:col-span-2">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-primary text-xs font-bold flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Display Currency</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed pl-8">
          Select your preferred currency symbol (USD $, EUR €, GBP £, INR ₹, JPY ¥, AUD A$, CAD C$, CHF Fr, SGD S$, AED د.إ) to dynamically format all monetary inputs, net gains, and break-even output metrics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* Worked ROI Examples Section */}
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Practical Walkthrough</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mt-1">Worked ROI Examples</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Step-by-step ROI calculations demonstrating how to compute returns for both asset investments and paid ad campaigns.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 not-prose">
      {/* Example 1: Financial Asset */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-5 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🏢</span> Example 1: Real Estate / Stock Investment
          </h3>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-500/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-emerald-500/20">Asset Growth</span>
        </div>
        
        <div class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted">
          <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> An investor purchases an index portfolio for <strong>$10,000</strong> and sells it <strong>3 years</strong> later for <strong>$15,000</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft rounded-xl border border-hairline-soft space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
          <div class="flex justify-between text-ink">
            <span>1. Net Profit Calculation:</span>
            <span class="font-bold">$15,000 - $10,000 = $5,000</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-ink">
            <span>2. Simple ROI Calculation:</span>
            <span class="font-bold">($5,000 / $10,000) × 100 = 50.00%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-primary font-bold pt-1 border-t border-hairline-soft">
            <span>3. Annualized ROI (CAGR):</span>
            <span>[($15,000 / $10,000)^(1/3) - 1] × 100 = 14.47% / yr</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Interpretation:</strong> While the cumulative return over 3 years is 50%, the annualized return of 14.47% reveals the true compounding growth rate per year, outperforming the historical S&P 500 average.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* Example 2: Marketing Campaign */}
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-5 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-3">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-ink flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📣</span> Example 2: Digital Marketing Campaign
          </h3>
          <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold text-primary bg-primary/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-primary/20">Marketing ROI</span>
        </div>
        
        <div class="space-y-2 text-xs text-muted">
          <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> An e-commerce brand spends <strong>$5,000</strong> on Meta Ads, generating <strong>$20,000</strong> in revenue. Product gross profit margin is <strong>40%</strong>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft rounded-xl border border-hairline-soft space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
          <div class="flex justify-between text-ink">
            <span>1. Gross Profit:</span>
            <span class="font-bold">$20,000 × 40% = $8,000</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-ink">
            <span>2. Net Profit After Ad Spend:</span>
            <span class="font-bold">$8,000 - $5,000 = $3,000</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-primary font-bold">
            <span>3. Marketing ROI (mROI):</span>
            <span>($3,000 / $5,000) × 100 = 60.00%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex justify-between text-muted pt-1 border-t border-hairline-soft">
            <span>4. Break-Even Revenue Target:</span>
            <span>$5,000 / 0.40 = $12,500</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          <strong>Interpretation:</strong> Looking strictly at gross sales ($20,000 / $5,000 = 4.0x ROAS) looks great, but incorporating the 40% gross margin shows that net marketing ROI is 60% with $3,000 in net profit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* ROI Interpretation & Benchmarks Table */}
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-4">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Performance Benchmarks</span>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mt-1">ROI Interpretation: What is a Good Return on Investment?</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted mt-1">Evaluating your ROI calculations against industry standards, risk levels, and alternative asset classes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-ink dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-sm text-body space-y-4">
      <p>
        Interpreting your ROI result requires context. A 20% ROI achieved over a 3-month ad campaign is extraordinary, whereas a 20% ROI over a 10-year real estate holding represents modest growth (~1.8% annually, below inflation). When evaluating ROI:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Positive ROI (> 0%):</strong> Indicates net profit. The capital return exceeded initial costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Break-Even ROI (= 0%):</strong> Total revenue generated exactly equals initial capital outlay and cost of goods.</li>
        <li><strong>Negative ROI (< 0%):</strong> Indicates financial loss. The cost exceeded final return proceeds.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-hairline bg-surface-card shadow-xs">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-canvas-soft text-ink font-semibold border-b border-hairline uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">
          <tr>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6">Asset / Channel Category</th>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6">Typical Expected ROI</th>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6">Time Horizon</th>
            <th class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6">Key Characteristics & Risk Profile</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline-soft text-body">
          {benchmarkTiers.map((tier) => (
            <tr class="hover:bg-canvas-soft/50 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6 font-semibold text-ink">{tier.category}</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6 font-mono font-bold text-primary">{tier.typicalRoi}</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6 text-muted">{tier.timeframe}</td>
              <td class="py-3.5 px-4 sm:px-6 text-muted leading-snug">{tier.notes}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* ROI vs ROAS Section with Contextual Internal Link */}
  <div class="p-8 rounded-2xl bg-surface-card border border-hairline space-y-6 shadow-sm not-prose">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">
      <span>⚖️</span> Comparative Guide
    </div>
    
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">ROI vs. ROAS: Key Differences & When to Use Each</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed">
        While both metrics measure financial return in digital marketing, mistaking <strong>ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)</strong> for <strong>ROI (Return on Investment)</strong> is one of the most common causes of unprofitable scaling.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 pt-2">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline-soft space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>📊</span> Return on Investment (ROI)
        </h3>
        <ul class="text-xs text-muted space-y-2 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Scope:</strong> Bottom-line net profitability.</li>
          <li><strong>Costs Included:</strong> Ad spend, Cost of Goods Sold (COGS), shipping, software, merchant fees, and team overhead.</li>
          <li><strong>Primary Metric:</strong> Net Profit / Total Investment Outlay.</li>
          <li><strong>Best Used For:</strong> Strategic executive decisions, annual marketing channel budget allocation, and business valuation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline-soft space-y-3">
        <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🎯</span> Return on Ad Spend (ROAS)
        </h3>
        <ul class="text-xs text-muted space-y-2 list-disc pl-4 leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Scope:</strong> Top-line advertising revenue efficiency.</li>
          <li><strong>Costs Included:</strong> Direct advertising cost (ad spend) only. Ignores product manufacturing and overhead.</li>
          <li><strong>Primary Metric:</strong> Gross Ad Revenue / Direct Ad Spend.</li>
          <li><strong>Best Used For:</strong> Campaign-level optimization, ad set bidding tactics, and creative testing on Meta, Google, and TikTok.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-primary/5 border border-primary/20 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink">Need campaign-level ad spend analysis?</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted">
          Calculate your exact ad spend efficiency, break-even ROAS targets, and profit margins with our dedicated tool.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a 
        href="/roas-calculator" 
        class="shrink-0 px-4 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white font-semibold text-xs rounded-lg hover:bg-primary/90 transition-all flex items-center gap-2 shadow-2xs"
      >
        <span>Try Break-Even ROAS Calculator</span>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* FAQ Section */}
  <section class="pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
    <FAQ faqs={faqs} title="Frequently Asked Questions (ROI Calculation)" description="Common questions about ROI formulas, marketing ROI, annualized returns, and ROI vs ROAS." />
  </section>

</section>

